  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Switch play through the middle",
  "description": "Play 7 v 7 on a pitch split into three zones. The defending team (red) is locked in the zones: two press in blue's back zone, two stay in the middle zone and two plus the keeper in their own defensive zone. Blue play freely and move up to get an overload in the middle and attacking zones.\n\nBlue must switch play at least once before they can score. A switch only counts if the ball has gone through the central corridor in one of the zones. If red win the ball they may counter and move freely in all zones. Blue have six attacks, then the teams swap roles.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "The midfielders get available in the space between red's forwards and midfielders."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Keep the width – the wide players stay wide so the switch opens up space."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Switch play when the opponents have shifted to the ball side."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "If you lose the ball – win it back as quickly as possible."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
